earlier run, or when a recording served a reply without its own draw key
(a repeat after the recording ran out of draws, or a recording made
without per-draw keys). Every request a run makes should therefore carry
the run's draw index. A \code{\link[=gr_mock_client]{gr_mock_client()}} keeps no cache, so under it an arm that
leaves the index out is not refused; under a cache it would be.

Every request is checked against \code{governor} before it is sent, for the
benchmark as a whole: each run's trace is held to the governor's call,
spending and token limits less what the runs before it used. A run ends
at its first refused request (the \code{hr_budget_refused} condition is caught
there), is recorded as \code{failure_kind = "budget_stop"} and counted wrong
(or \code{NA} on an item with no label, as below).
The runs after it are still started, so every row exists and the refusals
are visible; their requests are refused before anything is sent. With \code{governor = NULL} the limits are
read from \code{\link[=gr_options]{gr_options()}} when the benchmark starts and apply to the whole
benchmark, as they apply to one run of a reader.

An arm that raises an error has that run recorded as \code{"error"}, counted
wrong, with the message in the run's trace. Every run on an item with no
label has \code{correct = NA}, whatever its \code{failure_kind}: a failure on it
cannot count against an arm when a success could not count for it. Rows
on the \code{"dev"} split are
marked \code{reportable = FALSE}: dev is for tuning, and its scores are not
evidence. The reference is locked when scoring starts (see
\code{\link[=hr_reference]{hr_reference()}}).

Fewer than 5 runs warns (class \code{hr_few_runs}): with fewer, run-to-run
spread cannot be told from the differences between arms, and interval
reports are expected to refuse such a benchmark unless it is labelled
descriptive.

The arms run under a private random stream started from \code{seed}, so an arm
that samples gives the same draws on every call with the same seed, and the
caller's random state is left as it was.
